\nElections\nDepartments\nAuditor\nAssessor\nBoard of Commissioners\nCities\nCommunications\nCommunity Service\nEmergency Management\nExtension\nGeographic Information Systems (GIS)\nHighway\nHuman Resources\nEmployment\nJail\nPublic Health\nRecorder\nRSR Social Services Zone\nSheriff\nState’s Attorney\nTownships\nTreasurer\nVeterans\nWater Resources\nTaxpayer Information\nRichland County iTax\nRichland County Parcel Viewer\nContact Us\nWELCOME\nHome\nWELCOME\nHome\nBudget for 2027\nHomestead Tax Credit\nFlood Information\nExcess Property Sale\nForeclosure Properties\nMinutes/Agendas\nEmployment\nAbout Us!\nRichland County is located in the southeastern corner of North Dakota. It borders Cass County on the north, Ransom & Sargent Counties on the west, South Dakota to the south, and Minnesota to the east. Learn More\nPaying Your Property Taxes Online\nRichland County uses a service called “iTax” to process taxes. You can access it by going to the following internet address:\nhttps://itax.tylertech.com/RichlandND\nLocate your tax properties using the search function by entering your parcel number OR owner name (not both).\nClick the parcel number link in the TaxID-S column if multiple parcels are listed.\nTo view your statement, click on “Show Current Tax Bill”, or to make a payment, click on “Pay Taxes”.\nIf paying whole installments choose an amount from the cart options or enter a specific amount in payment box provided.\n*NOTE: When paying property taxes through Richland County iTax the following fees apply:\n-Debit or credit card 2.45% fee\n-Checking or savings account flat fee $1.50\nOur Facebook Feed\nGrab Your Calendars\n8:00 am, October 20, 2026 – Commission Meeting\n8:00 am – 9:00 am , October 20, 2026 – Water Resource District Board Meeting\n1:00 pm, October 27, 2026 – RSR Human Service Zone Board Meeting\n8:00 am, November 3, 2026 – Water Resource District Board Meeting\nNovember 11, 2026 – Courthouse Closed - Veteran's Day\nClick here for more calendar events!\nContact\n418 2nd Ave N | Wahpeton, ND 58075\nPhone: 701-642-7700 | Fax: 701-642-7701\nRichland County strives for the highest levels of compliance to ADA guidlines for website accessibility.\nClick here to see our accessibiliy statement.\nSearch\nSearch\nInterested in working\nfor Richland County?\nNotifications",
